## API Reference: REST API
- [REST API](https://support.datacite.org/reference/introduction.md)
- activities
  - [Get a JSON API result of activities.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_activities.md)
  - [Get a JSON API result of a specific activity.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_activities-id.md)
- client-prefixes
  - [Return a list of client-prefixes.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_client-prefixes.md)
- clients
  - [Return a list of clients (repositories).](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_clients.md)
  - [Return clients DOI production statistics.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_clients-totals.md)
  - [Return a client.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_clients-id.md)
  - [Return activities for a specific client.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_clients-id-activities.md)
- dois
  - [Return a list of DOIs.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_dois.md)
  - [Add a new DOI.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/post_dois.md)
  - [Return a DOI.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_dois-id.md)
  - [Update a DOI.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/put_dois-id.md): PUT requests to the /dois endpoint will update a DOI record if it already exists and create a new record if the DOI name is not already taken.
  - [Delete a DOI (for DOIs in draft state only).](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete_dois-id.md)
  - [Return activities for a specific DOI.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_dois-id-activities.md)
- events
  - [Return a list of events.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_events.md)
  - [Return an event.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_events-id.md)
- heartbeat
  - [Return the current status of the REST API.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_heartbeat.md)
- prefixes
  - [Return a list of prefixes.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_prefixes.md)
  - [Return prefixes DOI production statistics.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_prefixes-totals.md)
  - [Return a prefix.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_prefixes-id.md)
- provider-prefixes
  - [Return a list of provider-prefixes.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_provider-prefixes.md)
- providers
  - [Return a list of providers (including members and consortium organizations).](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_providers.md)
  - [Return providers DOI production statistics.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_providers-totals.md)
  - [Return a provider.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_providers-id.md)
  - [Return activities for a specific provider.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_providers-id-activities.md)
- reports
  - [A JSON array of reports.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_reports.md)
  - [Add a new report.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/post_reports.md)
  - [Return a report.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_reports-id.md)
  - [Update a report.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/put_reports-id.md)
- repositories
  - [Add a new repository.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/post_repositories.md)
  - [Update a repository.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/put_repositories-id.md)
  - [Delete a repository (only possible if no DOIs are in the repository)](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete_repositories-id.md)
- credentials
  - [Return a list of API keys for the authenticated repository account.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/get_credentials-api-keys.md)
  - [Create a new API key for the authenticated repository account.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/post_credentials-api-keys.md)
  - [Revoke an API key for the authenticated repository account.](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete_credentials-api-keys-id.md)

## API Reference: MDS API
- [MDS API](https://support.datacite.org/reference/mds.md)
- /dois
  - [Get URL for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/list-doi-name.md): Returns an URL associated with a given DOI.
  - [List all DOIs](https://support.datacite.org/reference/list-all-dois.md): Returns a list of all DOIs for the requesting Repository account. There is no guaranteed order.
  - [Create DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/create-doi-name.md): Registers a new DOI if the specified DOI doesn’t exist. This method will attempt to update the URL if you specify an existing DOI. Creating a DOI requires authentication credentials.Note that…
  - [Delete DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete-doi-1.md): Deletes a DOI if DOI is in **Draft** state.
- /metadata
  - [Get Metadata for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/create-metadata-record-1.md): Returns the most recent version of metadata associated with a given DOI.
  - [Create Metadata for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/create-metadata-record-2.md): Stores a new version of metadata. The request body must contain valid DataCite XML, or another supported metadata format. Authentication credentials are required.
  - [Delete Metadata for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete-metadata-record-for-doi-name.md): Changes a DOI from "Findable" to "Registered" state. To return the state to "Findable", PUT new metadata.
- /media
  - [Get Media for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/list-media-for-doi-name.md): This request returns list of pairs of media type and URLs associated with a given DOI.
  - [Create Media for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/list-media-for-doi-name-1.md): POST will add media type/URLs pairs to a DOI. Standard domain restrictions check will be performed.
  - [Delete Media for DOI](https://support.datacite.org/reference/delete-media-for-doi.md): DELETE will delete media type/URLs pair for a DOI.

